Directory-entry hashing
-----------------------

Files: src/nvfuse_dirhash.c and the accompanying include/nvfuse_dirhash.h interface.
Implementation source: e2fsprogs v1.43, lib/ext2fs/dirhash.c.
https://github.com/tytso/e2fsprogs/blob/v1.43/lib/ext2fs/dirhash.c

Copyright (c) 2001 Daniel Phillips
Copyright (c) 2002 Theodore Ts'o.
The TEA implementation also credits Jeremy Fitzhardinge (1998); that credit
and its GPL notice are retained in the source.

The identified upstream implementation is licensed under the GNU Library
General Public License, version 2 (LGPL-2.0-only). Section 3 explicitly allows
a given copy to be distributed under the ordinary GNU GPL, version 2. That
option is exercised for this distribution, which uses GPL-2.0-only notices.
COPYING.LIB supplies the original Library GPL text and the section 3 basis;
it does not offer this converted copy under LGPL or change upstream's license.

The hash implementation was checked against that upstream version. NVFUSE
adaptations include its u32/s32 types and includes, returning zero for an
unsupported hash version, and a redundant per-word padding reset. Hash
algorithms, seeds, results and the public function signatures are unchanged
by this licensing clarification, made on 2026-11-14. The upstream source is
the basis for this copy; historical local GPL version 3/commercial notices
are not being treated as permission to relicense someone else's GPLv3 code.

CRC32C hardware helpers
----------------------

File: CRC32C portion of src/nvfuse_dirhash.c.
Matching upstream helpers: Linux v2.6.32,
arch/x86/crypto/crc32c-intel.c.
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v2.6.32/arch/x86/crypto/crc32c-intel.c

Copyright (C) 2008 Intel Corporation
Authors: Austin Zhang <austin_zhang@linux.intel.com>
         Kent Liu <kent.liu@intel.com>
License: GNU GPL version 2 only.

NVFUSE adapts the helpers for userspace, its initial all-ones accumulator,
no final XOR, and local CPU probing; a portable software fallback is also
present. The upstream attribution is retained alongside that source portion.

Linux list and poison helpers
-----------------------------

Files: include/list.h and include/poison.h.
Matching reference: Linux v2.6.39, include/linux/list.h,
include/linux/poison.h and the list node declarations in include/linux/types.h.
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v2.6.39/include/linux/list.h
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v2.6.39/include/linux/poison.h
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v2.6.39/include/linux/types.h

These internal kernel headers are covered by that tree's GNU GPL version 2
license; COPYING supplies the license text. The referenced headers do not
contain individual copyright notices to reproduce. Existing comments remain.
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v2.6.39/COPYING

The poison header matches that reference apart from NVFUSE's non-Linux NULL
list poison pointers. List adaptations include local type declarations and
includes, new/new_first renamed for C++ compatibility, LIST_HEAD/container_of
definitions, selected prefetch changes, casts, and formatting. These are
matching upstream references, not a claim that the original import used that
exact tag. Neither header is being relicensed from a different upstream grant.

Bitmap helpers
--------------

File: src/nvfuse_dep.c, ext2fs_set_bit, ext2fs_clear_bit and ext2fs_test_bit.
Matching implementation: e2fsprogs v1.43, lib/ext2fs/bitops.c.
https://github.com/tytso/e2fsprogs/blob/v1.43/lib/ext2fs/bitops.c

Copyright (C) 1993, 1994, 1995, 1996 Theodore Ts'o.
C language equivalents written by Theodore Ts'o, 9/26/92.
Modified by Pete A. Zaitcev 7/14/95 for big-endian and non-32-bit systems.

The three implementations match after replacing upstream integer types with
NVFUSE aliases and ignoring formatting. The original license is GNU Library
GPL version 2. As for the directory hash copy, its section 3 option is exercised
for GNU GPL version 2 only in this distribution; COPYING.LIB retains the
original license. Existing NVFUSE author and date notices are preserved.

The former fuse_ext2-labelled Windows major/minor/makedev macro block was
removed during release preparation. It appeared after all functions, was used
nowhere in that translation unit, and exported no definitions to other files.
No fuse_ext2 implementation is retained in that block; this is not a claim
that the original three macro definitions were traced to a particular revision.

